From 7d0ae799b8b5320ad15d011ae8adfc4022574044 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 04:25:33 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(gateway): a subagent's answer no longer withdraws the
 chat's open question

Answering a background subagent's approval or question took the running turn's own clarify off every viewer while its tool kept waiting. A subagent prompt keeps the generation it was asked in, and both the answer (PendingControls.respond, with the generation the answer carries) and the subagent's own card retirement (the spawning turn runner's generation) withdrew every prompt of any other generation, so the chat's question published clarify.settled and left session.resume. The viewers showed a running clarify tool card with no form, and the agent waited the whole clarify timeout. Stale prompts are now withdrawn by the session's own execution generation.

A local chat (hub, TUI, Desktop) shows a question only as its viewers' card. When that card could not be registered (no session owner for the turn, a refused registration, a subagent whose chat is not live), the plain-text re-ask went to LocalSessionAdapter.send, which publishes nothing, was acknowledged, and the agent waited the clarify timeout. The local adapter now has no text fallback, and such a question returns at once with "[clarify prompt could not be delivered: the question could not be shown to the user]".
